# Declared trust base for the secp256k1 VST proof.
#
# `make axioms` runs `Print Assumptions` on every public body proof
# (audit/assumptions.v) and FAILS if any reported assumption is absent from
# this list.  Adding a line here is a deliberate, reviewed expansion of the trust
# base; an unexpected assumption means an axiom crept into the verified surface.
#
# Names are the fully-qualified identifiers exactly as Print Assumptions prints
# them.  One token per line; `#` starts a comment.

# --- Foundational (trusted toolchain: Coq stdlib + VST/floyd) ---------------
# Classical logic + extensionality that floyd's separation-logic automation rests
# on.  These come from the toolchain, not from this development.
# NB: [Print Assumptions] prints some of these with a shorter or fully-qualified
# name depending on what the gate file [Import]s; both spellings are whitelisted
# so the gate is robust to import-driven requalification (prop_ext /
# functional_extensionality_dep are VST/Coq's propositional + dependent functional
# extensionality, the same axioms as the qualified forms below).
